{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ubtq3fzH49ffKHNQRR3pn1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I now have a complete understanding of the pkg/testutils package. Let me provide a comprehensive report.\n\n## Analysis of pkg/testutils Package\n\nI've thoroughly examined the testutils package. Here's the complete breakdown:\n\n### 1. **DiffTest Struct Definition**\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5351/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (lines 46-55):\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string           // Identifies the subtest (used with t.Run)\n\tArgs          []string         // Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n\tStdin         []byte           // Input data for stdin; nil = EOF immediately, empty []byte = open stdin immediately closed\n\tEnv           []string         // Environment variables: KEY=VALUE pairs merged into inherited env (LC_ALL=C applied by default)\n\tWorkDir       string           // Working directory for binary execution; empty string defaults to t.TempDir()\n\tExitCode      int              // Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc   // Slice of normalization functions applied in order to stdout/stderr before comparison\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte // Post-execution file validation: relative path -> expected content\n}\n```\n\n**Key behaviors:**\n- `Stdin`: `nil` means both binaries receive EOF immediately. Empty non-nil slice `[]byte{}` also produces no bytes but represents an open stdin immediately closed\n- `Env`: Inherits the test process environment with `LC_ALL=C` applied as default override. Non-nil values merge KEY=VALUE pairs with matching keys overridden and new keys added\n- `WorkDir`: Defaults to `t.TempDir()` when empty\n- `Normalize`: Applied in sequence to both stdout and stderr before comparison; nil or empty means no normalization\n\n### 2. **RunDiffTests Function**\n\nSignature (lines 83-90):\n```go\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n```\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Executes each DiffTest as a named subtest using `t.Run(tc.Name, ...)`\n- Runs both `goBinary` and `refBinary` with identical inputs\n- Compares stdout, stderr, and exit codes between the two binaries\n- Fatal on divergence (test failure if outputs don't match)\n\nThe execution flow (lines 92-105):\n1. Resolves working directory (uses `t.TempDir()` if not specified)\n2. Builds environment (applies `LC_ALL=C`, merges test env)\n3. Runs both binaries with `runBinary()` capturing stdout/stderr\n4. Applies normalizers to both results in sequence\n5. Compares outputs with `compareOutputs()`\n6. Validates expected files with `checkExpectedFiles()`\n\n### 3. **BuildBinary Function**\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5351/pkg/testutils/build.go` (lines 16-27):\n\n```go\nfunc BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string\n```\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Compiles the Go package at `dir` using `go build`\n- Places the compiled binary in a temporary directory (automatically cleaned up when test completes)\n- Returns the path to the compiled binary\n- Fatals on build failure with error output\n\n**Implementation details:**\n- Resolves package name from directory path\n- Output binary placed at `filepath.Join(tmpDir, packageName)`\n- Executes `go build -o binPath dir` and captures combined output\n- Includes error context in fatal message if build fails\n\n### 4. **Normalization Mechanism**\n\n**Type definition** (lines 26-28):\n```go\ntype NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n```\n\n**TimestampNormalizer** (lines 66-72):\n- Built-in normalizer for timestamp-based tests\n- Replaces three common timestamp patterns with `<TIMESTAMP>` placeholder:\n  - Syslog format: `[A-Z][a-z]{2}\\s+\\d{1,2}\\s+\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}` (e.g., \"May 13 14:30:00\")\n  - ISO format: `\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\\s+\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}` (e.g., \"2026-05-13 14:30:00\")\n  - Time-only: `\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}` (e.g., \"14:30:00\")\n\n**Normalization flow** (lines 168-174):\n```go\nfunc applyNormalizers(res binaryResult, fns []NormalizeFunc) binaryResult {\n\tfor _, fn := range fns {\n\t\tres.stdout = fn(res.stdout)\n\t\tres.stderr = fn(res.stderr)\n\t}\n\treturn res\n}\n```\n- Applied to both stdout and stderr in sequence\n- Each normalizer receives the output from the previous one\n\n**ComposeNormalizers utility** (lines 232-238):\n```go\nfunc ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc\n```\n- Convenience function combining multiple normalizers into a single function\n- Returns a function that applies all provided functions in order\n\n### 5. **Exit Code Comparison**\n\nComparison logic (lines 176-185):\n```go\nfunc compareOutputs(t *testing.T, tc DiffTest, goRes, refRes binaryResult) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tstdoutMatch := bytes.Equal(goRes.stdout, refRes.stdout)\n\tstderrMatch := bytes.Equal(goRes.stderr, refRes.stderr)\n\texitMatch := goRes.exitCode == refRes.exitCode\n\tif stdoutMatch && stderrMatch && exitMatch {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tt.Fatalf(\"%s\", formatDivergence(tc, goRes, refRes))\n}\n```\n\n**Exit code extraction** (lines 130-148):\n- If command succeeds (no error), exit code is 0\n- If `exec.ExitError` is raised, actual exit code is extracted via `exitErr.ExitCode()`\n- Other errors (failure to start binary) cause fatal failure\n\n### 6. **Stdout/Stderr Capture and Comparison**\n\nBinary execution and capture (lines 107-128):\n```go\nfunc runBinary(\n\tt *testing.T, binary string, args []string,\n\tstdin []byte, env []string, workDir string,\n) binaryResult {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), defaultTimeout)\n\tdefer cancel()\n\tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, binary, args...)\n\tcmd.Env = env\n\tcmd.Dir = workDir\n\tvar stdout, stderr bytes.Buffer\n\tcmd.Stdout = &stdout\n\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n\tif stdin != nil {\n\t\tcmd.Stdin = bytes.NewReader(stdin)\n\t}\n\terr := cmd.Run()\n\tif ctx.Err() == context.DeadlineExceeded {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"binary %s timed out after %v\", binary, defaultTimeout)\n\t}\n\treturn extractResult(t, binary, err, stdout.Bytes(), stderr.Bytes())\n}\n```\n\n**Key features:**\n- 10-second timeout per binary execution (constant `defaultTimeout = 10 * time.Second`)\n- Captures stdout and stderr into separate `bytes.Buffer` instances\n- Stdin provided via `bytes.NewReader()` only if non-nil\n- Timeout fatals with the binary name and timeout duration\n- Returns `binaryResult` struct containing stdout, stderr, and exit code\n\n**Byte-level comparison** (lines 178-180):\n- Uses `bytes.Equal()` for exact binary comparison (no text normalization without explicit normalizers)\n- Compares captured bytes directly after applying normalizers\n\n**Divergence reporting** (lines 187-199):\n- Formats detailed divergence output showing:\n  - Command-line args\n  - Stdin (truncated if >256 bytes)\n  - Reference and Go binary stdout (in quoted form)\n  - Reference and Go binary stderr (in quoted form)\n  - Reference and Go binary exit codes\n\nAll functions follow the `t.Helper()` pattern for correct test failure attribution."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"edf60472-4efc-4511-8c9a-36f71bb61d1e","uuid":"19e9b56c-edb1-41d1-9d9a-73dba70d8eee","timestamp":"2026-05-20T13:24:45.306Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5351, I need to understand the pkg/testutils package. Read the main source files (testutils.go or similar) to understand:\n\n1. The DiffTest struct - all fields and their purpose\n2. The RunDiffTests function - how it compares Go binary vs reference binary output\n3. The BuildBinary function\n4. Any Normalize function or normalization mechanism\n5. How exit codes are compared\n6. How stdout/stderr are captured and compared\n\nSearch breadth: medium. Report the full DiffTest struct definition and the key function signatures with their behavior.","agentId":"a60895d11a2e44891","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I now have a complete understanding of the pkg/testutils package. Let me provide a comprehensive report.\n\n## Analysis of pkg/testutils Package\n\nI've thoroughly examined the testutils package. Here's the complete breakdown:\n\n### 1. **DiffTest Struct Definition**\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5351/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (lines 46-55):\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string           // Identifies the subtest (used with t.Run)\n\tArgs          []string         // Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n\tStdin         []byte           // Input data for stdin; nil = EOF immediately, empty []byte = open stdin immediately closed\n\tEnv           []string         // Environment variables: KEY=VALUE pairs merged into inherited env (LC_ALL=C applied by default)\n\tWorkDir       string           // Working directory for binary execution; empty string defaults to t.TempDir()\n\tExitCode      int              // Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc   // Slice of normalization functions applied in order to stdout/stderr before comparison\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte // Post-execution file validation: relative path -> expected content\n}\n```\n\n**Key behaviors:**\n- `Stdin`: `nil` means both binaries receive EOF immediately. Empty non-nil slice `[]byte{}` also produces no bytes but represents an open stdin immediately closed\n- `Env`: Inherits the test process environment with `LC_ALL=C` applied as default override. Non-nil values merge KEY=VALUE pairs with matching keys overridden and new keys added\n- `WorkDir`: Defaults to `t.TempDir()` when empty\n- `Normalize`: Applied in sequence to both stdout and stderr before comparison; nil or empty means no normalization\n\n### 2. **RunDiffTests Function**\n\nSignature (lines 83-90):\n```go\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n```\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Executes each DiffTest as a named subtest using `t.Run(tc.Name, ...)`\n- Runs both `goBinary` and `refBinary` with identical inputs\n- Compares stdout, stderr, and exit codes between the two binaries\n- Fatal on divergence (test failure if outputs don't match)\n\nThe execution flow (lines 92-105):\n1. Resolves working directory (uses `t.TempDir()` if not specified)\n2. Builds environment (applies `LC_ALL=C`, merges test env)\n3. Runs both binaries with `runBinary()` capturing stdout/stderr\n4. Applies normalizers to both results in sequence\n5. Compares outputs with `compareOutputs()`\n6. Validates expected files with `checkExpectedFiles()`\n\n### 3. **BuildBinary Function**\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5351/pkg/testutils/build.go` (lines 16-27):\n\n```go\nfunc BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string\n```\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Compiles the Go package at `dir` using `go build`\n- Places the compiled binary in a temporary directory (automatically cleaned up when test completes)\n- Returns the path to the compiled binary\n- Fatals on build failure with error output\n\n**Implementation details:**\n- Resolves package name from directory path\n- Output binary placed at `filepath.Join(tmpDir, packageName)`\n- Executes `go build -o binPath dir` and captures combined output\n- Includes error context in fatal message if build fails\n\n### 4. **Normalization Mechanism**\n\n**Type definition** (lines 26-28):\n```go\ntype NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n```\n\n**TimestampNormalizer** (lines 66-72):\n- Built-in normalizer for timestamp-based tests\n- Replaces three common timestamp patterns with `<TIMESTAMP>` placeholder:\n  - Syslog format: `[A-Z][a-z]{2}\\s+\\d{1,2}\\s+\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}` (e.g., \"May 13 14:30:00\")\n  - ISO format: `\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\\s+\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}` (e.g., \"2026-05-13 14:30:00\")\n  - Time-only: `\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}` (e.g., \"14:30:00\")\n\n**Normalization flow** (lines 168-174):\n```go\nfunc applyNormalizers(res binaryResult, fns []NormalizeFunc) binaryResult {\n\tfor _, fn := range fns {\n\t\tres.stdout = fn(res.stdout)\n\t\tres.stderr = fn(res.stderr)\n\t}\n\treturn res\n}\n```\n- Applied to both stdout and stderr in sequence\n- Each normalizer receives the output from the previous one\n\n**ComposeNormalizers utility** (lines 232-238):\n```go\nfunc ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc\n```\n- Convenience function combining multiple normalizers into a single function\n- Returns a function that applies all provided functions in order\n\n### 5. **Exit Code Comparison**\n\nComparison logic (lines 176-185):\n```go\nfunc compareOutputs(t *testing.T, tc DiffTest, goRes, refRes binaryResult) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tstdoutMatch := bytes.Equal(goRes.stdout, refRes.stdout)\n\tstderrMatch := bytes.Equal(goRes.stderr, refRes.stderr)\n\texitMatch := goRes.exitCode == refRes.exitCode\n\tif stdoutMatch && stderrMatch && exitMatch {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tt.Fatalf(\"%s\", formatDivergence(tc, goRes, refRes))\n}\n```\n\n**Exit code extraction** (lines 130-148):\n- If command succeeds (no error), exit code is 0\n- If `exec.ExitError` is raised, actual exit code is extracted via `exitErr.ExitCode()`\n- Other errors (failure to start binary) cause fatal failure\n\n### 6. **Stdout/Stderr Capture and Comparison**\n\nBinary execution and capture (lines 107-128):\n```go\nfunc runBinary(\n\tt *testing.T, binary string, args []string,\n\tstdin []byte, env []string, workDir string,\n) binaryResult {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), defaultTimeout)\n\tdefer cancel()\n\tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, binary, args...)\n\tcmd.Env = env\n\tcmd.Dir = workDir\n\tvar stdout, stderr bytes.Buffer\n\tcmd.Stdout = &stdout\n\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n\tif stdin != nil {\n\t\tcmd.Stdin = bytes.NewReader(stdin)\n\t}\n\terr := cmd.Run()\n\tif ctx.Err() == context.DeadlineExceeded {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"binary %s timed out after %v\", binary, defaultTimeout)\n\t}\n\treturn extractResult(t, binary, err, stdout.Bytes(), stderr.Bytes())\n}\n```\n\n**Key features:**\n- 10-second timeout per binary execution (constant `defaultTimeout = 10 * time.Second`)\n- Captures stdout and stderr into separate `bytes.Buffer` instances\n- Stdin provided via `bytes.NewReader()` only if non-nil\n- Timeout fatals with the binary name and timeout duration\n- Returns `binaryResult` struct containing stdout, stderr, and exit code\n\n**Byte-level comparison** (lines 178-180):\n- Uses `bytes.Equal()` for exact binary comparison (no text normalization without explicit normalizers)\n- Compares captured bytes directly after applying normalizers\n\n**Divergence reporting** (lines 187-199):\n- Formats detailed divergence output showing:\n  - Command-line args\n  - Stdin (truncated if >256 bytes)\n  - Reference and Go binary stdout (in quoted form)\n  - Reference and Go binary stderr (in quoted form)\n  - Reference and Go binary exit codes\n\nAll functions follow the `t.Helper()` pattern for correct test failure attribution."}],"totalDurationMs":24615,"totalTokens":26031,"totalToolUseCount":4,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2639,"cache_read_input_tokens":21300,"output_tokens":2087,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2639},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":2087,"cache_read_input_tokens":21300,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2639,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2639,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":3,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":1,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
